<title>USA: Freddie Mac to redeem $450 mln in debentures.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac to redeem $450 mln in debentures.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp said Tuesday that on June 24 it would redeem all outstanding amounts of four fixed-rate debenture issues totaling $450 million as follows.</p>
<p>	 Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip</p>
<p>	  Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number</p>
<p>     $185 million     6.655	05/20/99   3134A0K68</p>
<p>     $125 million     6.65	 04/15/99   3134A0B68</p>
<p>     $ 80 million     6.64	 05/21/99   3134A0L75</p>
<p>     $ 60 million     7.29	 09/24/01   3134A1BE9</p>
<p>Payment of principal plus interest accrued to the redemption date will be made to shareholders of record as of the close of business on June 23, 1997, Freddie Mac said.</p>
<p>Freddie Mac is a corporation chartered by Congress that buys mortgages from lenders and packages them into securities for investors.</p>
</text>
